<title>RUSSIA: TABLE-Russian M2 rises to 363.8 trln rbls July 1.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Russian M2 rises to 363.8 trln rbls July 1.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's M2 money supply rose to 363.8 trillion roubles ($62.6 billion) on July 1 from 339.4 trillion roubles on June 1, central bank first deputy chairman Sergei Aleksashenko told Reuters on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The figures mean M2 money supply grew 23.2 percent in the first half, compared with an 8.6-percent rise in consumer prices over the same period.</p>
